  {
    "id": "1939478954525798808",
    "author": {
      "id": "1725169104963657728",
      "username": "AztecaAlpaca",
      "name": "阿兹特克小羊驼",
      "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2019350943930937348/0z3zAknf_400x400.jpg",
      "verified": false
    },
    "text": "1.0时代，阅读本身都是小众的；2.0时代，大家都可以轻松阅读，但内容普遍碎片化；3.0时代，只要人愿意，几乎什么形式的内容都可以快速阅读。\n\n但是，思考与学习依然是更本质更稀缺的活动。人并不一定变得更聪明，因为这些这些阅读只是把“内容消费”从一种高端消费逐步变成了大众化消费。",
    "created_at": "2025-06-30T00:19:51.000Z",
    "metrics": {
      "like_count": 0,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": null,
      "quote_count": null,
      "view_count": null,
      "impression_count": null
    },
    "media": null,
    "entities": {
      "urls": [],
      "hashtags": [],
      "mentions": []
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "1939478950352429388",
    "author": {
      "id": "1725169104963657728",
      "username": "AztecaAlpaca",
      "name": "阿兹特克小羊驼",
      "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2019350943930937348/0z3zAknf_400x400.jpg",
      "verified": false
    },
    "text": "“阅读2.0”时代，有了社交媒体和手机。\n\n信息是碎片的，缺乏结构性和完整性。\n\n几乎所有的信息都是被推送的，而非我们主动选择的。只要我们有时间，就一定可以被各种信息填满。信息不再稀缺，而注意力变得稀缺。\n\n在这个时代，区别文本和视频等信息形态不大，不同类别的信息可以出现在同一个平台中。",
    "created_at": "2025-06-30T00:19:50.000Z",
    "metrics": {
      "like_count": 0,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": null,
      "quote_count": null,
      "view_count": null,
      "impression_count": null
    },
    "media": null,
    "entities": {
      "urls": [],
      "hashtags": [],
      "mentions": []
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "1939478952336318691",
    "author": {
      "id": "1725169104963657728",
      "username": "AztecaAlpaca",
      "name": "阿兹特克小羊驼",
      "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2019350943930937348/0z3zAknf_400x400.jpg",
      "verified": false
    },
    "text": "“阅读3.0”时代，刚刚铺开，只能窥其一隅。\n\n2.0时代被消灭的信息稀缺性彻底回不来了，而注意力稀缺性则越发严重。不同的信息形态的隔阂更加微小，大模型可以快速完成相互切换。\n\n历史上第一次，普通人有能力去快速处理长内容，“信息的结构”可以在创作端保留并高效地传送给读者。",
    "created_at": "2025-06-30T00:19:50.000Z",
    "metrics": {
      "like_count": 0,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": null,
      "quote_count": null,
      "view_count": null,
      "impression_count": null
    },
    "media": null,
    "entities": {
      "urls": [],
      "hashtags": [],
      "mentions": []
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "1939478945457664387",
    "author": {
      "id": "1725169104963657728",
      "username": "AztecaAlpaca",
      "name": "阿兹特克小羊驼",
      "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2019350943930937348/0z3zAknf_400x400.jpg",
      "verified": false
    },
    "text": "参考Andrej Karpathy对软件发展的划分，阅读也进入了3.0时代。\n\n纸质媒介时代是“阅读1.0”；基于社交媒体与手机的碎片化阅读是“阅读2.0”的形态；大语言模型则开启了“阅读3.0”时代。 https://t.co/ei0FhMvz9S",
    "created_at": "2025-06-30T00:19:49.000Z",
    "metrics": {
      "like_count": 3,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": null,
      "quote_count": null,
      "view_count": null,
      "impression_count": null
    },
    "media": null,
    "entities": {
      "urls": [
        {
          "url": "https://t.co/ei0FhMvz9S",
          "indices": [
            102,
            125
          ],
          "display_url": "x.com/feltanimalworl…",
          "expanded_url": "https://x.com/feltanimalworld/status/1939469231319388181"
        }
      ],
      "hashtags": [],
      "mentions": []
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "1939478948326658541",
    "author": {
      "id": "1725169104963657728",
      "username": "AztecaAlpaca",
      "name": "阿兹特克小羊驼",
      "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2019350943930937348/0z3zAknf_400x400.jpg",
      "verified": false
    },
    "text": "“阅读1.0”时代，我们主要从纸质媒介获得信息，信息的来源对大多数人来说是稀缺的，没得选，有啥看啥。这个时候很难把纸质内容与电视广播当成一回事，因为观感上差异太大。\n\n“博学”是一很难达到的目标，因为正常际遇下我们能够触及到领域就很少。\n\n我们不太可能被乱七八糟的信息干扰，阅读只属于少数人",
    "created_at": "2025-06-30T00:19:49.000Z",
    "metrics": {
      "like_count": 0,
      "retweet_count": 0,
      "reply_count": null,
      "quote_count": null,
      "view_count": null,
      "impression_count": null
    },
    "media": null,
    "entities": {
